<p>This week introduces two of the most powerful tools in Python programming: <strong>functions</strong> and <strong>data structures</strong>. You will learn how to define reusable functions with parameters and return values, understand variable scope, and work with Python's built-in data structures — lists, tuples, dictionaries, and sets. You will also learn list comprehension and essential built-in functions like <code>len()</code>, <code>range()</code>, and <code>sorted()</code>.</p>

